              { textOffset: 2144, responses: [0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0], nextTopics: [3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0] },
              { textOffset: 2264, responses: [0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0], nextTopics: [4, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0] },
            ],
            textPool: "Hello.  I am Derrida.  Pardon my appearance.\u0000What's going on?\u0000~1I sent for you, am I correct?  You have travelled thousands of miles and made your way through this building to bring me a package? ^1I did not request this package.  Moments ago you met the true recipient.  He appeared to be me, as he had when he sent for the package.  This is not a man -- it is an artificial organism, the D/Generation prototype.  ^1As a protective measure, D/Generation is trapped in a state of physical paralysis. However, it has managed to interface with the computer system, releasing the other organic weapons to cover its escape.  Then it sent for you.   ^1It knew that you would come, carrying the neurotransmitter that will reverse its paralysis.  And, indeed, that is what you have done.  You have brought D/Generation the means of its escape.\u0000Where are we?\u0000D/Generation is a demon, and this is its hell.  Even though it is paralyzed, it can conjure elaborate visual constructs much like the earlier Neogen weapons you have already seen.  We have long sought to create realities other than our own.   ^1D/Generation can, and this sensory deception is its sole weapon, a weapon of unimaginable power. ^1What you see around you is a hallucination, an alternate reality.  None of this exists.  And now, like me, D/Generation has trapped you here as it takes the package and weapons from your body back in the room where you still stand. ^1It wishes to escape the building into the outside world, where it can seamlessly blend in, moving through the human world without detection.  We designed D/Generation from its DNA up as a terrorist weapon.  It is the perfect assassin.   The consequences of its escape are unthinkable. ^1I had attempted to destroy D/Generation before it trapped me here.  In the communications room, I have turned the building's microwave antenna inward so that it points into the room.  You must lure D/Generation into this room and activate the beam as it crosses in front of the dish. ^1But first, you must escape from here. There is a security terminal guarding the exit door.  No one may escape until the passcode is entered.\u0000Where is the communications room?\u0000It is here, on the top floor, very close to the exit.  It is marked with a red arrow.\u0000What is the passcode?\u0000You must understand, that the moment I utter it, D/Generation will also know.  Your only hope is to catch D/Generation before it escapes the building. ^1Be ready.  When I speak the word, you must run. ^1The passcode is:  regeneration.\u0000",
